# Which UCLA ROMS namelist vocabulary each roms_gpu release reads.
#
# A release reads the namelist groups and keys of the UCLA ROMS release named
# here, plus its own optional groups below. Groups it does not read are
# ignored; a CPU feature switch it does not have stops the run at start-up
# (src/host/feature_guard.F90). From v0.1.2-beta, a key it does not know in a
# group it reads stops the run at start-up, naming the group (before, the rest
# of that group silently kept its defaults).
#
# Keys added in later UCLA ROMS releases that roms_gpu does not read (the run
# stops if they are present):
#   0.12.0  &cdr_lite_settings  cdr_carbonate_sensitivity_time_interpolation
#   0.13.0  &v_sponge_settings  v_sponge_trc
#
# Keys of UCLA ROMS after 0.14.0 (dev) that roms_gpu reads, so that a
# namelist written from its template runs:
#   &bgc_settings  bgc_physics_subcycle, bgc_physics_timestep (BGC tracer
#     subcycling, #428), and its testing keys bgc_subcycle_pos and
#     bgc_subcycle_diag. Subcycling is not on the GPU yet:
#     bgc_physics_subcycle = .true. stops the run at start-up; the other
#     three keys act only with it.
#   &marbl_biogeochemistry_settings  marbl_balance (#430), which ships MARBL
#     columns between CPU ranks and changes no result. Each GPU computes
#     the wet columns of its tile (&tile_settings balances them), so
#     .true. is ignored, with a start-up note.
#   &imex_igw_settings  the IMEX internal-wave step and its 'modal' open
#     boundary (#433, #434); keys and accepted values in the IMEX section
#     below.
#
# GPU-only additions: the optional group &tile_settings (tile balancing),
# &passive_tracers (n_passive, init_mode, write_passive), and in
# &param_settings the keys n, nsub_x, nsub_e and ntrc_bio.
#
# &rho0_settings rho0: read at run time and required, as in UCLA ROMS (a
# namelist without the group stops the run). Up to v0.1.3-beta roms_gpu fixed
# rho0 at build time (-DROMS_RHO0, default 1000) and stopped when the
# namelist differed.
#
# Surface restoring: UCLA ROMS selects it with cpp keys, which the GPU model
# cannot see; roms_gpu switches it on with GPU-only logical keys in
# &surf_frc_settings (default .false., bulk forcing only), and reads the
# coefficient from the same group as UCLA ROMS:
#   CPU cpp key        roms_gpu &surf_frc_settings   coefficient group (cm/day)
#   SFLX_CORR          sflx_corr = .true.             &sss_correction dSSSdt
#   QCORRECTION        qcorrection = .true.           &sst_correction dSSTdt
#   CFLX_CORR (MARBL)  cflx_corr = .true.             &dic_alk_correction dCdt
# A forcing file holding the restoring data (sss, sst, sDIC/sALK)
# while its switch is off gives a start-up warning. The restoring-flux
# output (&surf_flx_output_settings wrt_rstflx) is not on the GPU.
#
# Pressure fluxes for nesting: &calc_pflx_settings calc_pflx and
# pflx_timescale as UCLA ROMS (the group is optional here; absent means
# off). UCLA ROMS computes up/vp only when built with the DIAGNOSTICS cpp
# key; roms_gpu computes them whenever calc_pflx = .true., with the
# internal-tide pressure of ucla-roms eae883ee, writes up_<side>/vp_<side>
# to the child boundary file for objects whose output_vars name them, and
# keeps u_slow, v_slow, p_slow in the restart. pflx_timescale must be > 0
# when calc_pflx is on (the run stops otherwise).
#
# Sponge tuning for nested children: &sponge_tune_settings ub_tune (the CPU
# needs the SPONGE_TUNE cpp key as well; the GPU only the switch) tunes the
# inflow nudging of the open boundaries to the parent's up/vp of the
# boundary files; it needs calc_pflx = .true. (the run stops otherwise), as
# UCLA ROMS. wrt_sponge writes <output_root_name>_spn.<date>.nc every
# output_period_sponge (nrpf_sponge records per file): the child and parent
# fluxes and the coefficient of every open side, averaged over the period
# (sponge_avg) or of the output step, as UCLA ROMS with its fixes of
# 2026-11 (sponge-tune-pio-fixes). As UCLA ROMS's precheck, with restarts
# and wrt_sponge on, nrpf_sponge * output_period_sponge must be positive
# and divide output_period_rst (the run stops otherwise). The coefficients
# ub_west, ub_east, ub_south, ub_north are restart fields, written after
# the step's tuning (exact restarts), as in that version of UCLA ROMS.
#
# Implicit free surface (&implicit_fs, fs_mode = 'implicit'; absent or
# 'split': the split-explicit fast loop), as in ucla-roms
# implicit-fs-defaults. The settings (the five keys of UCLA ROMS's
# namelist template; defaults in brackets):
#   fs_mode     'split' | 'implicit'                                ['split']
#   fs_nsub     implicit sub-steps of dt/fs_nsub per step, 1..4     [2]
#   fs_rho_inf  spectral radius at infinite omega dt, in [0, 1)     [0.5]
#               (1, Crank-Nicolson, stops the run at the read)
#   fs_tol      relative residual of the elliptic solve             [1e-8]
#   fs_verbose  1: FS_SOLVE line per step; 2: + FS_VOL, FS_SRC,      [0]
#               FS_WALL lines (FS_SRC also with fs_mode = 'split')
# Solver and development settings: read as in UCLA ROMS, where the
# defaults are the recommended values, the keys may change between
# versions and C-Star and Forge do not expose them: fs_theta,
# fs_theta_div, fs_maxit (a solve that reaches it without meeting fs_tol
# stops the run), fs_precond, fs_mg_levels, fs_mg_nu, fs_mg_smoother,
# fs_mg_lag, fs_mg_faces, fs_drag_implicit, fs_warm, fs_tang_nudge,
# fs_cor_metric, fs_pot_time, fs_pg_rho, fs_flather_zghost (fs_rho_inf =
# 0, fs_nsub = 1, fs_pg_rho = fs_flather_zghost = .false. give the earlier
# single step); UCLA ROMS's MPI-layout keys fs_mg_gather, fs_mg_global_on
# and fs_exch_thin are read and not used, fs_selftest is read and ignored.
# GPU tuning settings (roms_gpu only): fs_gpu_gather, fs_gpu_coarse,
# fs_gpu_graph and fs_gpu_opt (layout and latency of the solve),
# fs_gpu_timers (timing runs: FS_COST, FS_WIN). fs_stress_time is no
# longer read (as in UCLA ROMS): a namelist that sets it stops at the
# read. Output files record fs_mode, and with 'implicit' fs_rho_inf and
# fs_nsub, as global attributes.
# Boundary options: roms_gpu's open edges have one barotropic type, UCLA
# ROMS's OBC_M2FLATHER (Flather normal faces, the zetabc sea level, the
# upwind tangential condition with inflow nudging), which the implicit
# free surface implements. The UCLA ROMS options for which the implicit
# step prints a start-up note there (OBC_M2ORLANSKI, open edges without an
# OBC_M2 type, OBC_Z2ORLANSKI, LEGACY_ORLANSKI, OBC_RAD_NORMAL, OBC_RAD_NPO)
# do not exist in roms_gpu, so it prints none.
# fs_gpu_opt is a bit mask in [0, 65535], default 65495 (was 471: bits
# 512 .. 32768 are new); bit 512 sums the PCG's partials of four ranks on
# one node in pairwise order instead of by MPI_Allreduce (GPU-only
# rounding-level difference), every other bit is bit-identical to 0. The
# solve stops the run on a NaN or Inf residual norm or <p,q>, with the
# CPU's message.
#
# IMEX internal-wave step (&imex_igw_settings present: on; absent: the
# stock step), as in ucla-roms #433 and #434 (IMEX_IGW with its 'modal'
# open boundary). The CPU's cpp key IMEX_IGW is the presence of
# the group here. The settings (the keys of UCLA ROMS's namelist
# template; defaults in brackets):
#   imex_verbose     0 quiet; 1 solver statistics (IMEX line,           [0]
#                    IMEX_SOLVE); 2 + the true FP64 residual of every
#                    solve (IMEX_PCHK) and max |dp|; same results
#   imex_bref_hours  rebuild interval (model hours) of the reference     [24]
#                    stratification b_ref, the operator, its
#                    preconditioner and the 'modal' boundary modes; 12
#                    for strongly evolving stratification
#   imex_rst_state   1 the IMEX state in the restart files (exact        [1]
#                    restart); 0 none (smaller files, inexact restart)
#   imex_obc_mode    normal velocity at open faces: 'modal' the     ['auto']
#                    characteristic (per-mode Flather) condition,
#                    implicit in the stage solves; 'fixed' the OBC's
#                    explicit value; 'auto' 'modal' when an open side
#                    exists and every open side has 3-D boundary data
#                    (normal velocity, temperature, salinity: the CPU's
#                    M3_FRC_BRY and T_FRC_BRY), else 'fixed' (decided at
#                    the first step and printed)
#   imex_obc_tref    'modal': time scale (s) of the reference m(z),  [259200]
#                    the low-passed baroclinic mismatch that is not
#                    radiated; 0 none; >= ~3 inertial periods at the
#                    open edges' lowest |f| and >= 1 d
# Solver and development settings: read as in UCLA ROMS, where the
# defaults are the recommended values, the keys may change between
# versions and C-Star and Forge do not expose them: imex_theta_p,
# imex_phi, imex_theta_c, imex_mu, imex_nu, imex_rho, imex_am3_crv (only
# 1/6 on the GPU), imex_tol_pred, imex_tol_corr, imex_maxit,
# imex_solver_enabled, imex_allow_explicit, imex_selftest (only 0 on the
# GPU), imex_n2_ref, imex_n2_taper, imex_warm (0, 1), imex_setup_lag,
# imex_pcg_start (0, 2, 3 on the GPU: 1 is CPU-only), imex_pcg_fused,
# imex_solver_prec, imex_stage_fused (only 1 on the GPU), imex_redu (only
# 0 on the GPU), imex_mix_split (0, 1), and of the boundary
# imex_obc_nmodes, imex_obc_q0 (0 off, or 0.2-1: sqrt(1 - f^2/omega0^2)
# where f/omega0 > 0.6 at the edges where the internal tide enters),
# imex_obc_cmin, imex_obc_mprint (OBCM/OBCF lines). The values the GPU refuses stop
# the run at start-up. GPU tuning settings (roms_gpu only; a namelist that
# sets one stops UCLA ROMS): imex_gpu_redu, imex_gpu_stage, imex_gpu_sweep
# (on: deterministic sums, the fused stage, the restructured operator
# sweep). 'modal' needs the fused solve (imex_pcg_start 2 or 3,
# imex_pcg_fused 1, imex_warm 1) with imex_gpu_stage and imex_gpu_sweep on
# (the defaults); with other values 'modal' stops and 'auto' runs 'fixed'
# with a note (the CPU would run 'modal', e.g. with imex_pcg_start 0).
# Keys removed from UCLA ROMS on 2026-11-13 (their former defaults are now
# fixed) stop the run at the read with a message that lists them; this
# GNU sed line deletes them, with their comment and value continuation
# lines, from a namelist file (the same line as in UCLA ROMS's
# src/namelist.nml):
# sed -E -i '/^[[:space:]]*(imex_force_mode|imex_n2_min|imex_bt_mode|imex_bt_passes|imex_s2d_check|imex_rhs_full|imex_probe_steps|imex_pcols|imex_win|imex_precond|imex_pcg_variant|imex_pcg_overlap|imex_adj_fused|imex_bref|imex_bref_floor|imex_bref_every|imex_bref_smooth|imex_n2_reg|imex_obc_rhs|imex_obc_op|imex_obc_zero|imex_obc_diag|imex_pred_btfix|imex_tsmix_n|imex_sponge_eq|imex_trim3d|imex_obc_eig|imex_obc_dcols|imex_obc_scrit|imex_obc_sband|imex_obc_fref|imex_obc_trelax|imex_obc_cslow|imex_obc_supercrit)[[:space:]]*[=(]/I{:a;$!{N;/\n([[:blank:]]*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_%]*[[:blank:]]*[=(]|[\/&$])[^\n]*|[[:blank:]]*|![^\n]*)$/!ba};/\n([[:blank:]]*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_%]*[[:blank:]]*[=(]|[\/&$])[^\n]*|[[:blank:]]*|![^\n]*)$/!d;s/^.*\n/\n/;D}' namelist.nml
# The free surface takes &implicit_fs as without IMEX (no IMEX-specific
# default). Restart files carry the IMEX state, the 'modal' reference m
# (imex_obcm) and 17 restart scalars as the CPU's; a file written with a
# removed option, or with other boundary settings (e.g. 'fixed' to
# 'modal'), is read as an inexact restart with a note.
#
# Half-resolution forcing: interp_bulk_frc, interp_flux_frc
# (&surf_frc_settings) and interp_bgc_frc (&bgc_settings) are read but not
# used; roms_gpu takes a forcing field as half resolution from its shape
# ((LLm/2 + 2) x (MMm/2 + 2) at rho points, xi one shorter at u points,
# eta one shorter at v points) and interpolates it as UCLA ROMS does with
# the key on. A field that fits neither the model grid nor these shapes
# stops the run.
#
# Per-tracer lists: &vertical_mixing_settings akt_bak and &tracer_diff2 tnu2
# accept one value per tracer, as in UCLA ROMS (up to 512), in its tracer
# order (T, S, nt_passive generic, CDR_LITE, MARBL). Only akt_bak's T and S
# entries are used (as on the CPU, the other tracers mix with salinity's
# diffusivity). tnu2 is used per tracer, as UCLA ROMS with TS_DIF2: each
# tracer's harmonic diffusivity is its tnu2 plus the v_sponge ramp. Generic
# passives added by the GPU-only &passive_tracers n_passive beyond nt_passive
# take salinity's tnu2.
#
# roms_gpu      UCLA ROMS namelist
